                <pb facs="0497" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v22/pg468"/>

                <head>136. Summary of a Presidential Review Committee Meeting<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d136-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            from="1979-06-18T13:30:00-04:00" to="1979-06-18T14:45:00-04:00">June 18,
                            1979, 1:30–2:45 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Vice President Mondale chaired a meeting to discuss the Indochina refugee
                    situation. The outflow from Indochina is growing rapidly, 30,000 last
                    month—60,000 this month. The outflow exceeds the capacity of the first-asylum
                    countries to absorb them on a temporary basis, and Malaysia, Thailand, and
                    Indonesia have all recently threatened not to admit additional refugees. The
                    refugee flow threatens the political stability of the countries involved and
                    introduces tensions in U.S. relations with the region. Henry Owen will prepare a
                    paper for the President suggesting initial measures to attempt to cope with the
                        problem.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d136-f2"/> (S)</p>
                <pb facs="0498" n="469" xml:id="pg469"/>
                <p>A State paper which served as the basis for the discussion is attached.</p>


                <xi:include href="d136-a1.xml" xpointer="d136-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d136-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d136-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Carter Library, National Security Affairs, Staff Material, Far East,
                    Platt Chron File, Box 67, 6/15–30/79. Secret. The meeting took place in the
                    Situation Room at the White House.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d136-f2" n="2" xml:id="d136-f2-content">
                <p>Presumably reference is to Owen’s June 21 memorandum to Carter. (Carter Library,
                    National Security Affairs, Staff Material, Office, Outside the System File, Box
                    53, Chron, 6/79)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
